            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0244" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5850: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-02T09:00:00+08:00">February 2, 1933—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 2—12:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>105. Following from Consul General Mukden: February 1, 4 p.m. According to
                    confidential information believed trustworthy 19 troop trains will move from
                    Chinchow to Suichung and Shanhaikwan February 2nd or 3rd.</p>
                <p>All indications point to Jehol drive starting within a few days when military are
                    expected to issue an official statement.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
